      "content": "KINGS LANGLEY          \tWATFORD ROAD TL 0702  \t\t\t\t\t(West side)                                       13/171                                  \tCedar Lodge -                                      \t\tII Lodge now a house. Early C19. Uncoursed knapped flint with stone quoins and dressings. Steep hipped red tile roof with toothed tiles. Central red brick chimney. Small flat roofed rear extension. A single-storey, small rectangular gate-lodge facing E at start of a drive to Langley Lodge. Symmetrical front with one window each side and central door. Square headed  2-light  casement windows with moulded wooden frames, pointed heads to each light and sunk spandrels. 4-centred arched doorway with carved keystone.  Battened door in pointed moulded frame.  One matching window on each end. Listing NGR: TL0743002068"
    }
  ],
